1
00:00:00,764 --> 00:00:02,432
You may have heard the phrase

2
00:00:02,432 --> 00:00:05,969
"in space, no one can hear you scream."

3
00:00:05,969 --> 00:00:07,404
(Laughter)

4
00:00:07,404 --> 00:00:10,374
But that's true only for human ears.

5
00:00:10,374 --> 00:00:14,978
The universe is filled with tenuous atmospheres of one kind or another,

6
00:00:14,978 --> 00:00:17,314
and through those atmospheres, pressure waves,

7
00:00:17,314 --> 00:00:19,449
sound moves

8
00:00:19,449 --> 00:00:24,488
through stars, across galaxies, even between galaxies.

9
00:00:24,488 --> 00:00:25,756
One of the most wonderful

10
00:00:25,756 --> 00:00:28,725
and recently discovered examples of cosmic sound

11
00:00:28,725 --> 00:00:33,230
is in the very young universe, shortly after the Big Bang.

12
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:37,634
Now you may be wondering, how would we know that?

13
00:00:37,634 --> 00:00:40,771
