15
00:00:43,106 --> 00:00:47,110
simply because it takes time for the light to get to you.

16
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:52,149
Remarkably, if you look far enough past all the galaxies,

17
00:00:52,149 --> 00:00:56,053
you can see to a time before any galaxies had yet formed,

18
00:00:56,053 --> 00:01:02,326
even to a time when the universe itself had only just been born.

19
00:01:02,326 --> 00:01:05,862
So what do you see coming from this newborn universe?

20
00:01:05,862 --> 00:01:11,301
You see the light of the Big Bang's hot, glowing youth.

21
00:01:11,301 --> 00:01:15,505
At that time, the universe was filled with an almost uniform,

22
00:01:15,505 --> 00:01:17,407
hot, glowing gas

23
00:01:17,407 --> 00:01:22,412
of atomic nuclei and electrons and intense light.

24
00:01:22,412 --> 00:01:28,452
