37
00:02:09,826 --> 00:02:12,863
around the full spherical dome of the sky,

38
00:02:12,863 --> 00:02:15,966
[a] bit like this image here.

39
00:02:15,966 --> 00:02:19,503
But as microwave telescopes became more sensitive,

40
00:02:19,503 --> 00:02:24,074
they began to see slight variations in brightness from place to place,

41
00:02:24,074 --> 00:02:27,711
so more recent images of the microwave sky

42
00:02:27,711 --> 00:02:32,115
appear completely covered in very slight patches.

43
00:02:32,115 --> 00:02:33,550
You can see them more clearly

44
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:37,087
in this blowup of a region that's about the size of your fist,

45
00:02:37,087 --> 00:02:39,089
